    {
      "id": 900,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        700
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 21,
      "mode": 0,
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX-2.5: Long Take (Context Windows)\n\nGenerate one continuous **20 second** take with a single `EmptyLTXVLatentVideo` pass.\n`LTXV Context Windows` patches the model so sampling runs in **4 overlapping windows**\n(145 frames each, 40 frames of overlap) and fuses them back, so the clip never exceeds the\nmodel's trained window length and never needs the whole 481-frame latent in attention.\n\n1. **Length** - 481 frames at 24 fps = 20.0 s. `context_length` / `context_overlap` are\n   *real* frames and must be `8n + 1`; internally 145 -> 19 latents, 40 -> 5.\n   The clip is 61 latents, so the early steps tile it in **4 windows**\n   (0-18, 14-32, 28-46, 42-60); the uniform schedule widens the overlap later in the run\n   and those steps use **5 windows** instead.\n2. **Context windows** - `standard_uniform` schedule spreads the overlap across sampling steps;\n   `pyramid` fuse blends the seams; `freenoise` shuffles window noise so the joins do not show.\n3. **Audio** - an `LTXVEmptyLatentAudio` of the same length is concatenated onto the video latent,\n   so the 20 s soundtrack is generated in the same pass and exported by `CreateVideo`.\n\nLonger clips = more windows, not more VRAM: each window is sampled at 145 frames, so peak VRAM\nstays flat. Fewer, longer windows mean fewer seams but a bigger per-window attention cost."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## LTX-2.5: Long Take (Context Windows)\n\nGenerate one continuous **20 second** take with a single `EmptyLTXVLatentVideo` pass.\n`LTXV Context Windows` patches the model so sampling runs in **4 overlapping windows**\n(145 frames each, 40 frames of overlap) and fuses them back, so the clip never exceeds the\nmodel's trained window length and never needs the whole 481-frame latent in attention.\n\n1. **Length** - 481 frames at 24 fps = 20.0 s. `context_length` / `context_overlap` are\n   *real* frames and must be `8n + 1`; internally 145 -> 19 latents, 40 -> 5.\n   The clip is 61 latents, so the early steps tile it in **4 windows**\n   (0-18, 14-32, 28-46, 42-60); the uniform schedule widens the overlap later in the run\n   and those steps use **5 windows** instead.\n2. **Context windows** - `standard_uniform` schedule spreads the overlap across sampling steps;\n   `pyramid` fuse blends the seams; `freenoise` shuffles window noise so the joins do not show.\n3. **Audio** - an `LTXVEmptyLatentAudio` of the same length is concatenated onto the video latent,\n   so the 20 s soundtrack is generated in the same pass and exported by `CreateVideo`.\n\nLonger clips = more windows, not more VRAM: each window is sampled at 145 frames, so peak VRAM\nstays flat. Fewer, longer windows mean fewer seams but a bigger per-window attention cost."
      }
    },
